<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet xml:id="exam3">
    <title>Exam 3 - MATH-262-02</title>

    <p>
        <alert>Instructions:</alert> You have 110 minutes to take this exam. Please answer each question in the space provided. Answers without justification may <alert> earn no credit </alert>. You are permitted your signed prep work journal and a calculator on this exam. No other notes or electronic devices of any kind are allowed on this exam. Failure to comply may result in earning a 0 on any portion of this exam and/or being reported to the university. 
    </p>

    <exercise workspace="2in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                [20 points] Use the <alert>definition</alert> of the Laplace transform to compute <m>\laplace{(t)}</m> where <md> f(t) = \begin{cases} t \amp 0 \leq t \lt 2; \\ 4 \amp t \geq 4. \end{cases} </md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace="1in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                [10 points] An LRC circuit consists of a 0.1H inductor, 3<m>\Omega</m> resistor, and a 0.05f capacitor. Suppose the circuit initially has no current or charge, but a switch is closed after 1 second that supplies the circuit with 100 V. The switch is opened again 2 seconds later. Write <alert> but DO NOT SOLVE</alert> a second-order IVP that models the charge in the circuit <m>q</m>.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                [12 points] Show that <m>x=0</m> is a regular singular point for the ODE <md>
                    2x^2(1+x)y'' + 3x(1+x)^3 y' - (1-x^2)y = 0.
                </md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace="3in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                [14 points] Compute <md>\lapinv{\frac{9+s}{4-s^2}}</md> by any method.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace="5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                [26 points] Use Laplace transforms to solve the IVP <md>u'' + u = \cos(3t); \ u(0)=1, \ u'(0)=0.</md> 
            </p>
        </statement>

        <hint>
            <p>
                <m> \int \cos(ax)\sin(t-x) \, dx = \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{\cos(t + (a+1)x)}{a+1} - \frac{\cos(t+(a-1)x)}{a-1}\right) </m>
            </p>
        </hint>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace="5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                [28 points] Find a power series solution centered at <m>x=0</m> to the ODE <md> (x-3)y' + 2y=0.</md> 
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    


</worksheet>
